"""Tool descriptions (MCP and /api/tools)."""
DOCS = {'lookup_rates': 'Negotiated rates for one billing code in one US state, one row per payer product, provider group (TIN) and price.\n\nArgs:\n    code: billing code, e.g. CPT/HCPCS "99213", "70553", MS-DRG "470"; a comma list works too\n    state: two-letter state where the provider practices, e.g. "TX" (Aetna: 3 networks nationwide)\n    payer: "cigna", "aetna", "uhc", a comma list, or "all"\n    network: optional filter on product/network/plan/employer name, e.g. "Choice Plus", "OAP", "UNITED AIRLINES"\n    city: optional practice city (NPPES), e.g. "Austin"\n    zip_prefix: optional ZIP prefix, e.g. "787" or "78701"\n    specialty: optional NUCC taxonomy text or code, e.g. "Orthopaedic Surgery", "Family Medicine", "207X00000X"\n    provider: optional TIN (9 digits), NPI (10 digits) or provider name\n    billing_class: optional "professional" or "institutional"\n    limit: max rows (default 200)\nReturns rows with payer, product, tin, provider, npis_in_area, rate, negotiated_type, billing_class, setting,\nmodifiers, place_of_service, medicare, pct_of_medicare.\nWhen `provider` is given, the provider\'s flat "all services" arrangements (code type CSTM-ALL, e.g. UHC\'s\nper-visit "PRO" rate for some urgent care groups) are included too. Radiology and other split services carry\nmodifier 26 (professional) / TC (technical) rows next to the global rate.', 'market_distribution': 'Distribution of negotiated rates for a code in a state: provider-group count, min/p10/p25/median/p75/p90/max,\nmean, Medicare amount and median % of Medicare. Each provider group counts once (its median published amount).\n\nArgs:\n    code: billing code, e.g. "99213"\n    state: two-letter state, e.g. "NY"\n    payer: "cigna", "aetna", "uhc", comma list, or "all"\n    network: optional product/network/plan filter\n    city: optional practice city\n    zip_prefix: optional ZIP prefix\n    specialty: optional taxonomy text or code (peer group)\n    billing_class: "professional" (default), "institutional" or "" for both\n    group_by: "payer" (default), "product", "setting" or "none"\n    place: "office" (default: base rates with no modifiers that apply in an office or anywhere),\n        "facility" (facility places of service) or "any" (every published amount, incl. modifiers 52/55/56/26/TC)\n    modifier: "" (unmodified/global rate, default), "26" (professional reading) or "TC" (technical component);\n        use this rather than run_sql for component-level distributions', 'provider_rates': 'FASTEST way to get one provider\'s rates for many codes (one call; use it instead of looping lookup_rates).\nRows collapse networks that pay the same amount; each row has payer, tin, code, modifiers (26 = professional\nreading, TC = technical, blank = global), negotiated_type, rate, medicare, pct_of_medicare, networks count.\nAlso returns the provider\'s flat all-services arrangements (code_type CSTM-ALL) if the payer uses one.\n\nArgs:\n    provider: NPI (10 digits), TIN (9 digits) or name; resolve names with search_providers first if unsure\n    codes: comma-separated billing codes (up to 50), e.g. "70450,70460,70551,71046"\n    state: two-letter state where the provider practices\n    payer: "cigna", "aetna", "uhc", comma list, or "all" (Aetna: 3 networks nationwide)\n    network: optional product/network filter', 'compare_providers': 'Side-by-side rates of several providers for several codes, per payer product (median of published amounts).\n\nArgs:\n    codes: comma-separated billing codes, e.g. "99213,99214,73721"\n    state: two-letter state\n    providers: comma-separated TINs, NPIs or provider names, e.g. "Baylor Scott,742664409"\n    payer: payer filter or "all"\n    network: optional product/network filter\n    place: "office" (default, base rates without modifiers), "facility" or "any"', 'benchmark_provider': 'How a provider\'s negotiated rates compare with peers in the same state (optionally same specialty):\nthe provider\'s rate, peer p25/median/p75, percentile rank and % of Medicare for each code and payer product.\nUse it for "how does my practice\'s contract compare" questions.\n\nArgs:\n    provider: TIN, NPI or name of the provider/practice\n    codes: comma-separated billing codes\n    state: two-letter state\n    payer: payer filter or "all"\n    specialty: optional peer specialty (taxonomy text or code)\n    network: optional product/network filter\n    place: "office" (default, base rates without modifiers), "facility" or "any"', 'network_breadth': 'How many clinicians (NPIs) and TINs in an area have published rates in each payer product/network,\nand their share of all NPPES clinicians there. Use for comparing network breadth.\n\nArgs:\n    state: two-letter state\n    specialty: optional taxonomy text or code, e.g. "Cardiovascular Disease"\n    city: optional practice city\n    zip_prefix: optional ZIP prefix\n    payer: payer filter or "all"\n    group_by: "product" (default) or "network"', 'provider_networks': 'Which payer products a provider has published rates in (by NPI, TIN, or name + state).\n\nArgs:\n    provider: NPI (10 digits), TIN (9 digits) or name\n    state: two-letter state (required when searching by name)', 'find_plans': 'Find networks by product, plan or employer name (Aetna publishes plan/employer names; Cigna and UHC name\nfiles by product), e.g. "Choice POS II", "MCKESSON", "Options PPO", "OAP".\n\nArgs:\n    query: text to search\n    payer: payer filter or "all"', 'list_products': 'The payer products (network families) loaded, with network and plan counts.\n\nArgs:\n    payer: payer filter or "all"', 'search_providers': 'Search clinicians/organizations in NPPES (by NPI, or name/specialty/city within a state) and show the TINs\npayers list them under. Use to resolve a provider name to NPI/TIN before other tools.\n\nArgs:\n    name: provider or organization name (substring)\n    state: two-letter state (required unless npi is given)\n    specialty: taxonomy text, e.g. "Dermatology"\n    city: practice city\n    npi: a 10-digit NPI\n    limit: max rows', 'code_info': 'Which payers publish a billing code, its type, published text where licensable (CPT text is withheld),\nand national Medicare physician fee schedule amounts.\n\nArgs:\n    code: billing code', 'medicare_rate': 'Medicare physician fee schedule amounts (CY2026, non-facility and facility) for comma-separated HCPCS/CPT\ncodes: national ("US") or adjusted by the state\'s mean locality GPCI.\n\nArgs:\n    codes: comma-separated codes, e.g. "99213,99214"\n    state: two-letter state or "US" (national)', 'data_status': 'What data is loaded (payers, products, networks) and whether the app is ready.', 'rank_providers': 'Rank provider groups (TINs) by negotiated rates across a basket of codes, in one state or NATIONALLY\n(state "US", every state). Each group\'s rate per code is its median published office/base rate; the basket is\ncombined as a weighted average (dollars) and a weighted average % of national Medicare. Use it for questions like\n"highest-paid radiology groups in the nation" (codes = the specialty\'s common CPTs, weights = their relative\nvolume if known). National runs cover Cigna and UHC by default (Aetna\'s national files are heavy).\n\nArgs:\n    codes: comma-separated billing codes (up to 20), e.g. "70450,70553,71250,72148,74177,77067"\n    state: two-letter state, a comma list of states, or "US" for national (default). A national run that\n        runs out of time lists states_not_done in the first (summary) row: call again with those and merge\n    payer: "cigna,uhc" (default), "cigna", "uhc", "aetna" or "all"\n    specialty: optional filter on the group\'s main NPPES classification, e.g. "Radiology"\n    weights: optional comma-separated weights in the same order as codes (e.g. annual volumes); default equal\n    place: "office" (default), "facility" or "any"\n    modifier: "" (global/unmodified, default), "26" (professional reading) or "TC" (technical)\n    min_codes: minimum codes a group must have rates for (default: half of the codes)\n    limit: how many top groups to return (default 25)', 'run_sql': 'Run ANY read-only DuckDB SQL over the price data, for questions the other tools do not answer (custom rankings,\nweighted baskets, cross-payer or cross-state comparisons, histograms, joins with Medicare...). Write one SELECT\n(CTEs allowed). Data is pulled in with table functions that take quoted string arguments only:\n\n  rc_rates(\'<payers>\', \'<states>\', \'<codes>\' [, \'<specialty>\' [, \'<place>\']])\n      Provider-group-level negotiated rates, one row per state x payer product x group x code x price.\n      payers: \'cigna\', \'uhc\', \'aetna\', a comma list or \'all\'. states: \'MO\', \'MO,KS\' or \'US\' (all 52).\n      codes: comma list, up to 30. specialty: optional filter on the group\'s main NPPES classification\n      (e.g. \'Radiology\'); use it for national queries, it makes them much faster. place: \'any\' (default, every\n      published row), \'office\' (base rates, no amount-changing modifiers, office or anywhere) or \'facility\'.\n      Columns: state, payer, product, pg (group id, unique within a payer), tin, provider (group name),\n      specialty, npis_in_area, tin_wide, code, negotiated_type (\'negotiated\',\'fee schedule\',\'derived\',\n      \'percentage\',\'per diem\'), rate (dollars; a percent when negotiated_type=\'percentage\'), rate_raw (as\n      published), billing_class (\'professional\'/\'institutional\'), setting, modifiers (e.g. \'26\',\'TC\',\'\'),\n      pos (comma list of place-of-service codes, \'\' = any), expiration.\n      A group practicing in several states appears once per state: for national per-TIN stats use\n      DISTINCT payer, tin, code, rate (or aggregate per state first). Payers publish placeholder amounts\n      ($0.01, $99,999.xx, $999,999.xx): exclude them with rate > 0.01 AND rate < 99999.\n  rc_medicare(\'<state>\')     Medicare physician fee schedule CY2026: hcpcs, modifier (NULL = global, \'26\', \'TC\'),\n                             status, state, nonfacility_amount, facility_amount, conversion_factor, year.\n                             \'<state>\' = \'US\' (national) or a state (mean locality GPCI).\n  rc_codes(\'<payers>\')       code index: payer, billing_code_type, billing_code, name, published_rows.\n  rc_products(\'<payers>\')    networks: payer, net, product, label, n_plans, plan_names, file_names.\n  rc_groups(\'<payers>\', \'<states>\')      groups practicing in the states: payer, state, pg, tin, tin_type,\n                             tin_wide, business_names, n_npi, name, cities, specialty.\n  rc_group_npis(\'<payers>\', \'<states>\')  payer, state, pg, npi (clinicians of each group located there).\n  rc_nppes(\'<states>\')       NPPES (up to 6 states): state, npi, name, entity_type, credential, city, zip5,\n                             taxonomy_code, taxonomy, classification, specialization.\n  rc_code_file(\'<payer>\', \'<code>\')      the raw per-code file (ps, ns, price fields), for debugging.\n\nExample, highest-paid radiology groups nationally on a weighted basket (weights = relative volume):\n  WITH r AS (SELECT DISTINCT payer, tin, provider, code, rate\n             FROM rc_rates(\'cigna,uhc\', \'US\', \'70450,71250,74177,72148\', \'Radiology\', \'office\')\n             WHERE negotiated_type IN (\'negotiated\',\'fee schedule\',\'derived\') AND rate > 0.01 AND rate < 99999),\n       w(code, wt) AS (VALUES (\'70450\', 3), (\'71250\', 2), (\'74177\', 4), (\'72148\', 2)),\n       m AS (SELECT hcpcs AS code, nonfacility_amount AS mcr FROM rc_medicare(\'US\') WHERE modifier IS NULL),\n       g AS (SELECT payer, tin, any_value(provider) provider, code, median(rate) rate FROM r GROUP BY ALL)\n  SELECT payer, tin, provider, count(*) n_codes, sum(rate * wt) / sum(wt) AS weighted_rate,\n         100 * sum(rate * wt) / sum(mcr * wt) AS pct_of_medicare\n  FROM g JOIN w USING (code) JOIN m USING (code) GROUP BY ALL HAVING count(*) >= 3\n  ORDER BY pct_of_medicare DESC LIMIT 25\n\nLimits: the call has about 4 minutes in total and ~1 GB of memory; national rc_rates over many codes is the\nslow part (fewer codes and a specialty filter keep it fast). If time runs out before every state is loaded,\n`notes` says which states were skipped: run again for those states. Results return at most max_rows rows.\nA missing rate means "no published rate", never "out of network". Percentages are not dollars.\n\nArgs:\n    sql: one SELECT statement using the rc_* table functions above (DuckDB SQL dialect)\n    max_rows: rows to return (default 500, at most 5000)\nReturns columns, rows, truncated, built (rows loaded per rc_rates call), notes (skipped states, missing files).'}
